Thank you for using Micro Clip Studio (the “App”). This Policy explains how information is collected, used, stored, and protected.

### 1. Information We Collect
The App is primarily **local / on-device** and does not require an account.

**1.1 Content you create (stored on device)**  
Including scripts and scenes, ideas and copy, material notes, publish plans, reminders, titles/tags, checklists, and attachments. This content is stored locally on your device to provide App features.

**1.2 Permission-based access (only after you grant permission)**  
- **Camera**: live preview and guides in Composition Assist; we do not upload camera frames without your action.  
- **Photos**: pick cover backgrounds/reference images, or save covers to your library.  
- **Notifications**: local reminders for publishing/creation. You may disable them in system or App settings.

**1.3 Preferences**  
Language, theme, font size, notification toggles, etc., stored locally.

**1.4 Advertising-related data**  
The App may show ads from third-party networks (e.g. Pangle). Ad SDKs may process device/ad-delivery data under their policies. The App is configured **not to request IDFA**; see the ad provider’s privacy policy for details.

### 2. How We Use Information
Only to: provide creation and planning features; remember preferences; show ads (if enabled); and support basic stability—not to sell personal information.

### 3. Storage and Transfer
- Creative content is stored **on device by default**.  
- Backup/export/share happens only when you choose, via system share sheets or files you save.  
- Ad requests may involve network communication handled by the ad provider.

### 4. Sharing
We do not sell personal information. Sharing may occur only with your consent/action, via ad SDKs as needed for ads, or when required by law.

### 5. Third Parties
Third-party ad SDKs may process data under their own policies (e.g. Pangle). Your use of those services is subject to their terms.

### 6. Your Choices
Manage permissions in iOS Settings; change in-App preferences; delete the App to remove local App data (back up first); contact us with privacy questions.

### 7. Children’s Privacy
The App is intended for creators/adults. We do not knowingly collect children’s personal data. Contact us if you believe such data was collected.

### 8. Updates
We may update this Policy and will post the revised version with a new effective date.

